{{Stealnotes
| name = Stone Remnant
| desc = However, abilities acquired from {{H|Earth Spirit}} can utilize the same Stone Remnant and the {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{A|Earth Spirit|Enchant Remnant|text=Enchanted Target}}.
| is_unacquirable = yes
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Stone Remnant
| desc = Stone Remnant is not {{H|Earth Spirit}}'s {{M|innate}} ability.<br><br>Requires drafting {{A|Earth Spirit|Magnetize}} to unlock this ability.
}}

 * This {{M|innate}} ability is in the {{Spellslot|4|6}}.
** {{Symbol|Charges}}
*** Kaolin begins the game with {{#var:Stone Remnant charges}} [[charges]], and the max charges value is defined as:
**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|{{#var:Stone Remnant charges}} + [[wikipedia:Floor and ceiling functions|⌊]] SelfLvl / {{#var:Stone Remnant type2 value1}} [[wikipedia:Floor and ceiling functions⌋|⌋]] , MAX {{=}} {{#expr:{{#var:Stone Remnant charges}}+floor(30/{{#var:Stone Remnant type2 value1}})}}}}
** {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|earth_spirit_stone_caller_innate}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Attack Damage|Bonus}}
*** Grants flat {{M|bonus attack damage}} based on the Kaolin's current {{M|main attack damage}}, values are periodically checked and the bonus values are updated immediately.
*** The ability effects are applied as follows:
***# The ability cast utilizing the {{Symbol|Stone Icon}} Remnant-unit.
***# Grants {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|earth_spirit_stone_caller_innate}} as a timed buff that grants the flat additional {{M|bonus attack damage}}, and is defined as:
***#* {{cf|expr}} {{Code|%Bonus[[Attack Damage|AtkDmg]] {{=}} {{#var:Stone Remnant type3 value1}} + {{#var:Stone Remnant value1}} × RemainingCharges}}
***#* Reapplying the buff does not stack, but refreshes its duration.

* Has the following targeting functionalities:
** {{Symbol|Target|Point}}
*** When point-targeted, Kaolin {{M|turns}} and casts the ability at the point-targeted direction.
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**** {{M|Doubletap}} places one Stone Remnant {{#var:Stone Remnant type1 value1}}-distance in front of Kaolin according to his {{M|facing angle}}.

* {{Symbol|Stone Icon}}
** Can only be destroyed in the following conditions:
*** Upon expiration.
*** Upon collision with the {{A|Earth Spirit|Rolling Boulder}} {{M|projectile}}.
*** Upon the {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{A|Earth Spirit|Enchant Remnant}} expiring.
*** Upon the {{A|Earth Spirit|Magnetize}} stone shatter delay duration.
** {{Symbol|fx|v}}
*** Can be seen through the {{M|Fog of War}} by everyone.
*** Abilities utilizing Stone Remnants are visible to everyone.
** {{Symbol|fx|s}}
*** Abilities utilizing Stone Remnants are audible to everyone.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Stone Remnant icon0}}
| desc = Call a Stone Remnant to the target location.  Stone Remnants have no vision and are invulnerable, and can be used with Earth Spirit's abilities.  Calling a Stone Remnant consumes a charge, which recharge over time. Stone Remnant has 7 charges.<br><br>Earth Spirit passively gains 3% bonus damage per unused Stone Remnant charge, and gains an additional 7.5% bonus damage for 10s when a Stone Remnant is targeted with an ability (does not stack).
}}
* {{Symbol|Stone Icon}}
** The unit is an unselectable and uncontrollable {{M|ward-type unit}}.
** There are no limits to the number of Stone Remnants created in the game.

